585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The gut microbiome is a vast ecosystem within our digestive system, made up of trillions of bacteria, viruses, fungi, and other microorganisms. These microbes, primarily located in the large intestine, play a critical role in maintaining digestive health, immune function, and even mental well-being. The microbiome is unique to each person, like a fingerprint, shaped by factors such as diet, genetics, environment, and lifestyle. What is the Gut Microbiome?: The gut microbiome consists of diverse microorganisms living in harmony with our body, influencing digestion, metabolism, and disease resistance. Why It Matters: A balanced microbiome helps with efficient digestion and nutrient absorption, produces vitamins, and protects against harmful pathogens.)
/E (The gut microbiome is a vast ecosystem within our digestive system, made up of trillions of bacteria, viruses, fungi, and other microorganisms. These microbes, primarily located in the large intestine, play a critical role in maintaining digestive health, immune function, and even mental well-being. The microbiome is unique to each person, like a fingerprint, shaped by factors such as diet, genetics, environment, and lifestyle. What is the Gut Microbiome?: The gut microbiome consists of diverse microorganisms living in harmony with our body, influencing digestion, metabolism, and disease resistance. Why It Matters: A balanced microbiome helps with efficient digestion and nutrient absorption, produces vitamins, and protects against harmful pathogens.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
