592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Diversity within the microbiome is crucial for maintaining a resilient and adaptable digestive system. Greater diversity generally means the gut is better equipped to handle various foods, resist pathogens, and support immune function. Reduced diversity has been linked to obesity, inflammatory bowel disease, and even mental health disorders. Diversity and Disease Resistance: A more diverse microbiome can defend against pathogens more effectively, preventing infections and inflammation. Microbiome Changes Through Life: The microbiome is influenced by birth \(vaginal vs. C-section\), breastfeeding, diet, antibiotics, and aging. Lifestyle factors such as diet and stress management play a crucial role in maintaining microbiome diversity.)
/E (Diversity within the microbiome is crucial for maintaining a resilient and adaptable digestive system. Greater diversity generally means the gut is better equipped to handle various foods, resist pathogens, and support immune function. Reduced diversity has been linked to obesity, inflammatory bowel disease, and even mental health disorders. Diversity and Disease Resistance: A more diverse microbiome can defend against pathogens more effectively, preventing infections and inflammation. Microbiome Changes Through Life: The microbiome is influenced by birth \(vaginal vs. C-section\), breastfeeding, diet, antibiotics, and aging. Lifestyle factors such as diet and stress management play a crucial role in maintaining microbiome diversity.)
