/ActualText (Hydrate Throughout the Day: Water is essential for digestion, nutrient absorption, and elimination. Start your day with a glass of water and stay hydrated by drinking water consistently throughout the day.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
888 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1342 0 R
/ActualText (Mindful Eating: Eating slowly and chewing thoroughly gives the digestive system time to process food, aids in nutrient absorption, and reduces bloating and gas. Aim to eat without distractions and focus on the flavors and textures of each meal.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
889 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1343 0 R
/ActualText (Incorporate Fiber and Fermented Foods: A diet rich in fiber \(from fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and legumes\) and fermented foods \(like yogurt, kefir, sauerkraut, and kimchi\) can nourish gut bacteria and promote regularity. Fiber feeds beneficial bacteria, while fermented foods add beneficial bacteria to your gut.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
